
Usage:
        sonda <command>
        sonda -T <target> [flags]
        sonda --update | --upgrade | --version | -h | --help

Commands:
        sys (default)         Show system information (CPU, memory, devices, etc.)
        net                   Show network information (interfaces, active connections, etc.)

Targets:
        pkgs                  List all installed packages
        cpu                   CPU information
        gpu                   GPU and graphics card information
        disks*                Disk and storage information (requires sudo for detailed partition info)
        memory                Memory information (requires sudo for detailed memory usage)
        kernel                Kernel boot parameters and loaded modules
        devices               PCI and USB devices
        network               Network interfaces and active connections
        battery               Battery status and power information
        boot                  Boot time analysis, warnings, and errors
        security              Security baseline (firewall, SELinux/AppArmor, SSH, encryption)
        all                   All available system and network information (long output)

Flags:
        
        -v                    Set the output verbosity level (min -v. max -vvv)
        -s, --save            Save the output to a log file in ~/.logs/sonda/
        -nc, --no-color       Strip color codes from output

Meta:
        --update              Check if updates are available (does not update)
        --upgrade             Update the Sonda tool to the latest version
        --version             Display the version of the Sonda tool
        --recommends          Check required and recommended system settings
        --banner              Display a colorful banner to add at the top of your shell rc file
        -h,--help             Show this help message and exit

Examples:
        sonda net
        sonda -T cpu
        sonda -T all -s -nc -v8
        sonda --update

!NOTES: All targets requireS -T, flags can be used with any target and only with -T.